1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,730
Advanced Class

2
00:00:01,730 --> 00:00:03,560
Jan. 14th (Tues.)
 Class Duty: Minazuki

3
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:06,980
Isaki and I are thinking 
of becoming two separate humans.

4
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:09,190
Separate humans?

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,260
Yes.

6
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:13,300
At first, the plan was 
to become one human,

7
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:17,490
to stop living a halfhearted 
existence as a werewolf...

8
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,500
But after talking things over,

9
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:25,790
we don't see a need to merge 
into a single personality.

10
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:29,140
Does that mean you'll 
each have your own body?

11
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,050
Yes.

12
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:32,340
Is that even possible?!

13
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:37,740
When we enrolled, the director 
told us that was an option.

14
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:39,270
Really?

15
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:44,650
I used to think it'd be better 
if I didn't exist.

16
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,830
But after starting 
an exchange diary with Isaki,

17
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,860
we want to be there for each other.

18
00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:50,510
I see.

19
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:54,950
Sure, I'll discuss it 
with the principal and director.

20
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:56,780
Thank you very much!

21
00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:00,390
So what will you do 
after you become humans?

22
00:01:00,390 --> 00:01:04,530
Until now, you were planning to enter 
a private liberal arts university.

23
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:07,230
But now with two Ohgamis 
in need of a career path...

24
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,240
Huh?

25
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,010
Eh?

26
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:11,970
Oh, no, Mr. Hitoma.

27
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:15,470
I didn't think about that at all!

28
00:01:16,130 --> 00:01:16,830
Ah...

29
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:53,170
Episode 6

30
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:53,170
Episode 6

31
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:53,170
The Misanthrope and the Light of Dawn

32
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:53,170
The Misanthrope and the Light of Dawn

33
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:51,520
Jan. 17th (Fri.)
Class Duty: Usami

34
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:51,520
Okay,

35
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,980
let's talk about the final
assignments for the advanced class.

36
00:02:55,690 --> 00:03:00,530
In order to graduate and become human, 
you need to pass the final assignment.

37
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:05,480
The principal and director will prepare 
a personalized task for each of you.

38
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,960
None of that matters to me.

39
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:12,420
I got 150 points deducted 
for sneaking off campus.

40
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:15,630
So there's no point in doing 
the final assignment.

41
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:18,030
"The final assignment

42
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:22,590
is meant to challenge you
in ways that a class can't teach."

43
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,320
Or so the principal said.

44
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:30,020
Graduation or not, 
you'll have to do the assignment.

45
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,440
You have until the end 
of February to submit it.

46
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:35,830
I want you all to do 
your best to complete it.

47
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:45,120
We've just received our final 
assignments from the principal.

48
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:50,060
Mine is to hunt down 
one of the director's gems.

49
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,500
A treasure hunt?

50
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,410
This contains hints to the gem's location.

51
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:58,090
Final Assignment
 Kyoka Minazuki

52
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,630
Oh? Now that sounds like a fun time.

53
00:03:58,650 --> 00:04:00,340
As for me,

54
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:04,230
I have to collect the signatures of 
every enrolled student and faculty member.

55
00:04:04,230 --> 00:04:05,240
Signatures?

56
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,300
So they just write down their names?

57
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:08,810
They're treating me like I'm stupid.

58
00:04:08,810 --> 00:04:10,020
This should be easy.

59
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:15,250
Mine is writing the sports anthem 
for our field day next year.

60
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,620
Sounds perfect 
for a music lover like you.

61
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:26,810
I have to write a 20,000-character novella
with a cast of five or more people.

62
00:04:28,110 --> 00:04:31,350
<i>None of the assignments 
seem overly difficult.</i>

63
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:37,550
<i>Instead of the end of February, 
we might see everyone finish in January.</i>

64
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:42,880
Jan. 24th (Fri.)
Class Duty: Minazuki

65
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:42,880
How are you all doing 
on your final assignments?

66
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:45,050
Pretty good, if you ask me.

67
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:47,590
I'm done with the melody 
and the lyrics for the chorus.

68
00:04:47,590 --> 00:04:50,680
You're working on the lyrics 
and music at the same time?

69
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,680
I wanted to nail the chorus first 
since it's the key part,

70
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,400
and then build out the rest from there.

71
00:04:56,670 --> 00:04:59,460
Huh, now that's an interesting approach.

72
00:04:59,890 --> 00:05:01,360
How about you, Usami?

73
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,280
I've already talked to every student.

74
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:05,450
But it's impossible.

75
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:07,410
What do you mean?

76
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:08,860
Take a look.

77
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:11,560
Are these... paw prints?

78
00:05:12,410 --> 00:05:16,530
The beginner class is still getting 
used to their human forms,

79
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:18,930
and a lot of the students can't write yet.

80
00:05:18,930 --> 00:05:23,910
I got their paw prints, but the principal
said they don't count as signatures.

81
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:26,840
The beginner class won't be easy...

82
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,380
How are you doing, Ohgami?

83
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:33,140
Why would they say this?

84
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:36,730
Why? I can't understand how they feel!

85
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,070
Sounds like you're struggling, too.

86
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:41,440
How's your assignment going, Minazuki?

87
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:46,150
The first hint was a crossword puzzle, 
which I found hard but managed to solve.

88
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:47,610
I see.

89
00:05:47,910 --> 00:05:51,090
The next one's just as difficult, 
and I'm still figuring it out.

90
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:53,830
I'm sure I'll manage to get it, though!

91
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:55,950
Since I solved the first one.

92
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:57,070
Yeah.

93
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:00,910
There's still more than a month left.

94
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,920
Don't stress out and panic.

95
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,790
Just keep on chipping away. Got it?

96
00:06:05,790 --> 00:06:06,800
Yes!

97
00:06:07,110 --> 00:06:09,470
Jan. 31st (Fri.)
Class Duty: Ohgami

98
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:09,470
There we go!

99
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,850
Music and lyrics, all done!

100
00:06:12,850 --> 00:06:15,340
I'm glad to hear it, Haneda.

101
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:20,440
Once I show it to the principal and 
get his okay, I'll finish the assignment!

102
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,150
Splendid work, Tobari!

103
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:26,440
You did it! You're the first one!

104
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:29,620
I'm mad that you beat me to it.

105
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,410
Still, congratulations.

106
00:06:31,410 --> 00:06:34,760
Thanks. How are you all doing?

107
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:40,470
I'm giving lessons every day for the 
beginner class to teach them to write.

108
00:06:40,470 --> 00:06:43,920
My story's over 20,000 characters now.

109
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,770
You sure did work hard, Ohgami.

110
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:48,290
So you're done now?

111
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:52,840
Actually, the plot's gotten too big!

112
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:53,670
What?

113
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:56,390
The cast has taken on a mind of their own,

114
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:58,850
with no ending in sight 
after 20,000 characters!

115
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:01,170
I don't know when I'll ever finish!

116
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:03,770
I see. That sounds rough.

117
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:05,960
What about you, Kyoka?

118
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:10,160
I'm ashamed to say 
that I've made no progress.

119
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:13,120
I see. Want me to help?

120
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,860
No, that won't be necessary.

121
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,820
This is my assignment.

122
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,580
I'll see through it all by myself.

123
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,930
Got it.

124
00:07:22,930 --> 00:07:25,300
Well, let us know if you need anything.

125
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,420
We're here to help.

126
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,130
Thank you for your concern.

127
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,430
Feb. 7th (Fri.)
Class Duty: Minazuki

128
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:35,890
I've finished!

129
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,980
A novella with a minimum of 20,000

130
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:39,550
characters and a cast of five or more!

131
00:07:39,550 --> 00:07:41,030
It's complete!

132
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:44,910
The final character count is 38,033!

133
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:47,020
Good job, Ohgami.

134
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:51,730
I think I might enjoy 
coming up with stories.

135
00:07:51,730 --> 00:07:53,220
That's great!

136
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:55,870
It's embarrassing to ask, 
but would you care to read it?

137
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:56,410
Sure!

138
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,830
Feb. 14th (Fri.)
Class Duty: Usami

139
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:01,390
Signature Book

140
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:01,390
Sui Usami

141
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,870
I'm done...

142
00:08:00,870 --> 00:08:05,040
I spent so much time teaching them 
to write, day in and day out.

143
00:08:05,430 --> 00:08:07,040
Some ran away.

144
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:09,300
Some were scared.

145
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:11,260
Some set up traps for me.

146
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:12,920
What a royal pain.

147
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,970
I see. You worked really hard.

148
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:17,690
Um...

149
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:20,570
Kyoka, how's your assignment going?

150
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:28,520
I mean, if there's anything I can do,
please don't hesitate to ask for help!

151
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,300
You're too kind.

152
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:36,740
That said, it's my assignment, 
so I'll do my best by myself.

153
00:08:38,870 --> 00:08:41,870
I learned the hard way!

154
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:45,880
If you don't put your feelings into words,
they won't get through!

155
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:51,020
So perhaps I may be acting out of line...

156
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:55,100
But if you need help, 
feel free to ask at any time!

157
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:02,350
Yes, I'll ask when the time is right.

158
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:06,730
Kyoka!

159
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:09,420
Tell me what part 
you're having trouble with!

160
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,250
I'll help you out!

161
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,810
Thank you for offering.

162
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:18,740
However, this assignment is 
for me to solve, so I'll be just fine.

163
00:09:19,530 --> 00:09:20,830
I can tell it's fake.

164
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:22,300
What?

165
00:09:22,710 --> 00:09:26,370
I've never liked the way you smile.

166
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:30,960
It reminds me of the person I love, 
forcing a smile on her face.

167
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:38,210
I simply hold pride 
in always staying positive.

168
00:09:38,210 --> 00:09:42,720
Forced as it may be, it is my wish 
to challenge myself and overcome this.

169
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,310
So there's no problem at all.

170
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:46,520
That attitude's what ticks me off!

171
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:48,760
Usami.

172
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,730
It's fine, Mr. Hitoma.

173
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:57,190
Is the point of this assignment 
not to overcome it yourself?

174
00:09:57,910 --> 00:10:03,660
I appreciate the concern you've shown me, 
but please understand.

175
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:08,520
You always try and handle 
everything on your own.

176
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:13,880
Will you be able to ask for help 
when you really need it?

177
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,420
I...

178
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:21,350
I have no need for your help.

179
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:25,640
Feb. 21st (Fri.)
Class Duty: Haneda

180
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:28,760
<i>One week left until the deadline.</i>

181
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:31,510
<i>Will Minazuki be okay?</i>

182
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,880
Mr. Hitoma!

183
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,330
Morning!

184
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:35,920
Ah, Ohgami.

185
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:38,300
Wait, is today the full moon?

186
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:41,870
Kyoka and Ushami are fighting, no cap?

187
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:47,010
What do you make 
of the situation with Kyoka?

188
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:57,260
I think it's important to admit 
when you can't do something by yourself.

189
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,590
I see...

190
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:00,720
In that case...

191
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:03,690
Mr. Hitoma, you ever takopa'd?

192
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:05,110
Takopa?

193
00:11:08,510 --> 00:11:13,270
I couldn't find octopus on short notice, 
so there's konjac in it instead.

194
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:18,490
There isn't any seafood in konjac,
so I can eat without hesitation.

195
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:24,760
The idea's that if you chat while 
cooking and eating all together,

196
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:27,450
you can ask about real 
heavy stuff, no prob!

197
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:29,770
No prob, huh?

198
00:11:29,770 --> 00:11:31,290
Plan number one.

199
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:37,500
Make Kyoka think that I have zero clue,
and figure out where she's stuck.

200
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:41,550
Hey, how's the assignment going, Kyoka?

201
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:43,970
<i>Right off the bat?!</i>

202
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,910
I'd say I'm making progress.

203
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:50,330
Oh, for real?

204
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:53,510
What's your assignment, anyway?

205
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:56,840
Mine is a treasure hunt.

206
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,340
Sounds like fun!

207
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,910
What do you do?

208
00:11:59,910 --> 00:12:02,630
You solve puzzles one by one.

209
00:12:02,630 --> 00:12:05,450
So it's not just one problem?

210
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:07,660
That's right.

211
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:14,620
The first one was a crossword puzzle, 
and the solution was "Gotemba".

212
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:24,530
Final Assignment

213
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:16,580
Isaki's heard of that!

214
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,550
They have an outlet mall there!

215
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:22,110
And? What's the second problem?

216
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:25,970
Oh, well, you see...

217
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:25,970
Final Assignment
 Kyoka Minazuki

218
00:12:27,290 --> 00:12:31,020
Wait, is the second 
one, like, <i>super</i> hard?!

219
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:33,600
Some kinda crazy math problem?

220
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:36,930
Isaki just can't with math!

221
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:40,650
The second appears 
to be some sort of riddle.

222
00:12:41,370 --> 00:12:42,620
It says...

223
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:49,280
<u>Final Assignment   Problem 2</u>

224
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:49,280
m 0 0 l 230 0 l 230 215 l 0 215

225
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:49,280
Try and remember!
The very first class!
And when you trace them in order...?

226
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,550
Try and remember.

227
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:45,980
The very first class.

228
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:49,280
And when you trace them in order...

229
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,060
That's what it says.

230
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:57,740
I looked up the first class for beginner, 
intermediate, and advanced levels,

231
00:12:58,350 --> 00:13:00,210
but I couldn't figure it out.

232
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:04,420
What was our first class 
for the beginner level?

233
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:06,360
A tour of the school.

234
00:13:06,810 --> 00:13:10,340
After the tour, they handed out 
a hiragana worksheet.

235
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:12,360
And then we introduced ourselves.

236
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:17,170
The beginner class starts by learning 
about writing and speaking.

237
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,350
That's right.

238
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:23,100
Kyoka, do you remember 
our first introductions?

239
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:25,150
Our first introductions?

240
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:29,380
Your name and the reason 
you want to be human.

241
00:13:31,910 --> 00:13:38,020
I want to become human to repay 
the kindness a human showed me.

242
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:44,120
That's why I also want to 
help the people around me.

243
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,060
And so...

244
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:50,140
Kyoka, I'm sorry about what I said!

245
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:51,090
What?

246
00:13:51,430 --> 00:13:56,100
I wasn't thinking about how you felt, 
wanting to do your best.

247
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:59,000
I just wanted to help.

248
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,030
For my own satisfaction.

249
00:14:01,570 --> 00:14:03,070
Usami...

250
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:05,330
No, don't say that.

251
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,890
You're not at fault here, Usami.

252
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:11,180
I should also...

253
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,200
Well...

254
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,080
Minazuki.

255
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:16,990
You know...

256
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:21,080
I can't do anything 
without depending on others.

257
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:27,170
Even for stuff I was asked to do, 
I often find I can't do it alone.

258
00:14:28,330 --> 00:14:34,140
I think it's a really important skill to 
be able to ask others when that happens.

259
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:39,260
No human can survive all on their own.

260
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:44,200
We bother those around us, 
as they bother us.

261
00:14:44,570 --> 00:14:47,510
Life is all about supporting 
each other in that way.

262
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:52,280
Is it really all right?

263
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:00,250
Would it be all right for me to ask you 
for your precious time?

264
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:03,420
I already said it was okay.

265
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,590
Fine by me as well.

266
00:15:05,590 --> 00:15:08,010
Yeah! You betcha!

267
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,220
Everyone...

268
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,680
Oh, don't forget I'm here, too.

269
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:17,390
That goes without saying, Mr. Hitoma!

270
00:15:18,970 --> 00:15:23,100
Everyone, please lend me your assistance!

271
