m 0 0 l 230 0 l 230 215 l 0 215

328
00:16:56,610 --> 00:17:02,650
Where was the confession?

329
00:16:56,950 --> 00:17:02,660
The final problem asks, 
"Where was the confession?"

330
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:04,540
What?!

331
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:07,620
Isaki, does that ring a bell?

332
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:09,630
I-I-Isaki?!

333
00:17:09,630 --> 00:17:11,130
I-If you ask Isaki...

334
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:13,220
Well...

335
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:16,990
Mr. Hitoma...

336
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:17,510
What?!

337
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:20,570
Wait, did you and Isaki...

338
00:17:20,570 --> 00:17:23,230
I don't know what you're thinking, 
but you're wrong!

339
00:17:23,230 --> 00:17:24,850
At least I think so!

340
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:28,800
Hey! You say something, too, Ohgami!

341
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:31,100
Isaki can't talk here...

342
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:32,630
Why not?!

343
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:36,670
This is Isaki we're 
talking about, not Isaki!

344
00:17:36,670 --> 00:17:39,160
Isaki can't just go blabbing about it!

345
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,850
What's this all about?

346
00:17:40,850 --> 00:17:46,980
Actually, the novel that Isaki wrote 
for her graduation assignment...

347
00:17:47,790 --> 00:17:50,710
Isaki can't say any more!

348
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:56,720
Isaki will go back to being 
Isaki tomorrow, so ask Isaki then!

349
00:18:00,390 --> 00:18:04,990
In my novel, it took place 
under the cherry tree.

350
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:06,890
Let's all look for it!

351
00:18:06,890 --> 00:18:08,350
Time to hunt for treasure!

352
00:18:08,350 --> 00:18:09,900
Hey, wait, everyone!

353
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,480
Make sure you don't go 
beyond the cherry tree!

354
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,010
Minazuki!

355
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:27,090
I see it. Up there!

356
00:18:30,390 --> 00:18:31,880
A treasure chest.

357
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:34,700
It sure is high up.

358
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,380
Will it come falling down if we shake it?

359
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,800
Let me give it a try.

360
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:39,380
There!

361
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,300
You suck.

362
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:45,790
How about we throw something at it?

363
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,890
Like a game of darts or target practice.

364
00:18:47,890 --> 00:18:49,730
That's an excellent suggestion!

365
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:52,670
Excuse me.

366
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:59,650
Could I possibly impose upon you to use 
that feather to knock the chest down?

367
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,280
That's no good!

368
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:03,580
How could you?!

369
00:19:04,490 --> 00:19:06,810
No need to be so formal.

370
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:09,870
Ask a little more casually, 
and I'd be happy to.

371
00:19:10,510 --> 00:19:11,920
Casually?

372
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:15,350
You sounded so pompous, 
it caught me off guard.

373
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,030
Pompous?

374
00:19:18,770 --> 00:19:21,260
Tobari, can you grab that box for me?

375
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:22,930
Sure thing!

376
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,020
Okay, here goes nothing.

377
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:26,640
Yes!

378
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:29,560
There!

379
00:19:30,230 --> 00:19:31,310
You did it!

380
00:19:38,370 --> 00:19:39,440
Oh, no! The barrier!

381
00:19:40,110 --> 00:19:42,110
Minazuki, stop!

382
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:48,750
Mr. Hitoma!

383
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:50,780
Are you hurt?

384
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,920
No, I'm fine.

385
00:19:53,870 --> 00:19:55,840
The box is safe as well!

386
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:04,030
Thank you so much.

387
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:12,640
Congratulations!

388
00:20:14,190 --> 00:20:19,190
Looks like everyone in the advanced class 
has finished their final assignments!

389
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:30,370
Principal, my apologies 
for taking so long.

390
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:34,830
I would not have been able to 
complete this assignment alone.

391
00:20:35,390 --> 00:20:40,800
However, I was able to see it through 
thanks to my wonderful friends.

392
00:20:41,350 --> 00:20:42,630
As such...

393
00:20:43,350 --> 00:20:49,100
Please distribute my points equally among 
the four of us in our class.

394
00:20:50,050 --> 00:20:51,890
Once again...

395
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:55,980
Congratulations!

396
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:02,650
With this, all of your graduation 
assignments have been submitted.

397
00:21:03,390 --> 00:21:09,560
And we have decided which students meet 
the requirements to graduate.

398
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:14,220
We will have one student 
graduating this year.

399
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:18,560
She has no violations on record, 
and has consistently acquired points.

400
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:25,300
A student with the clear academic 
and social skills to survive among humans.

401
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:29,830
However, she could never muster 
the courage to rely on others.

402
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:34,360
A student adamant on doing 
everything by herself.

403
00:21:35,910 --> 00:21:40,600
But by relying on others 
for her graduation assignment,

404
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:44,570
she finally learned to become a bother.

405
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:50,530
For these reasons stated, 
the one graduating will be...

406
00:21:52,890 --> 00:21:54,540
Kyoka Minazuki.

407
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,960
You're the one.

408
00:22:00,070 --> 00:22:01,850
Thank you very much!

409
